decision: changes-requested

Three defects remain:

- **F21 — medium:** Successful Git warnings are discarded below the history threshold, allowing unreadable graph metadata to report `ok`.
- **F22 — low:** Empty HEAD trees below the threshold report a check instead of being excluded.
- **F23 — low:** The displayed manual repair omits `--max-new-filters=-1`, so it can leave the recommendation unresolved.

Rules applied: feature review workflow, backend-go, security, documentation-style and delivery-evidence. I inspected the implementation, tests, CI, validation metadata and prior findings. I used sealed test evidence; no builds, repairs, repository edits or attestations were performed.

